  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Why 3 of these buy you 1 of those",
      "text": "Three quarters of the depth runs in linear time with a constant-size state; the remaining quarter provides exact lookup. The model is roughly a long-context recurrence with periodic attention checkpoints — which is a different bet from Gemma-4, where every layer is still attention and only the window shrinks.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "qwen35.hf",
          "lines": [
            764,
            768
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "Qwen3_5DecoderLayer.__init__",
            "first": "self.block_type = config.layer_types[layer_idx]",
            "sha": "6b267d68",
            "span": [
              761,
              771
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "What the serving path uses",
      "text": "vLLM does not use this transformers class. It imports GatedDeltaNetAttention from vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn_linear_attn.py and manages the conv and recurrent states as mamba-style cache tensors — which is why Qwen3.5/3.8 need a mamba-capable cache mode to serve at all.",
      "code": [
